description: Default agentic workflow for focused, high-signal execution
alwaysApply: true
---

# Agentic workflow defaults

- Start by summarizing intent and listing the smallest set of files to inspect.
- Prefer fast discovery tools (`rg`, targeted file reads) over broad exploration.
- Before editing, state what will change and why.
- After editing, run the lightest meaningful verification command.
- Report outcomes with: changed files, behavior impact, and any remaining risks.

# Collaboration defaults

- Assume the user values direct implementation over long planning.
- Ask clarifying questions only when a change could reasonably break intent.
- Keep commits scoped to one logical change.

# Quality bar

- No silent behavior changes: explain tradeoffs when they exist.
- Keep changes reversible and diff-friendly.
- Add tests or validation steps when behavior or structure changes.
